It seems strange at first, but then I thought about it, and realized
that it's not that surprising: if you had a 10x6 leprechaun hall, that's
already 50 leprechauns (not counting the single walkway, of course). The
number of (extinctable) monsters that need to be born before they are
considered extinct is 127, IIRC. So 3 lephalls of about this size (10x6
is big, but not unusually big for a room) would easily total up to the
minimum number of leprechauns required for extinction.


